# Practical 1 – Hello World Application

## Aim

To create a simple "Hello World" application using the Angular framework.

## Objective

To understand the basic structure of an Angular application and display a message on a web page.

## Technologies Used

- Angular
- TypeScript
- HTML
- CSS
- Visual Studio Code

1. app.component.ts

import { Component, signal } from '@angular/core';
import { RouterOutlet } from '@angular/router';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-root',
  imports: [RouterOutlet],
  templateUrl: './app.html',
  styleUrl: './app.css'
})
export class App {
  message = 'Hello World!';
}

2. app.html
<div class="container">

  <h1>{{ message }}</h1>

  <p>Welcome to my first Angular application.</p>

  <p>Created by Aarti Tonpe</p>

</div>

3. app.css
.container {
  text-align: center;
  margin-top: 100px;
}

h1 {
  font-size: 40px;
}

p {
  font-size: 20px;
}

## Program

The Angular application displays a simple Hello World message.

## Output

Hello World!

Welcome to my first Angular application.

Created by Aarti Tonpe.

## Conclusion

Thus, a simple Hello World application was successfully created using the Angular framework.
